@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8081

# Supply browserToken and adminToken in your HTTP client's private environment.
# Copy sessionId from the Start Session response into that environment.
# See the root README for disposable local credentials.

### Public health — 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Unauthenticated admin read — 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/logs

### Browser denied admin read — 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{browserToken}}

### Start session — 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/session/start
Authorization: Bearer {{browserToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "bank.example.test"
}

### Ordinary password focus — Safe / ALLOW
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/analyze
Authorization: Bearer {{browserToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
  "eventType": "password_focus",
  "actionType": "sensitive_action",
  "pageCategory": "sensitive_page",
  "formSubmitCount": 1
}

### Unsupported browsing field — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/analyze
Authorization: Bearer {{browserToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
  "eventType": "page_view",
  "url": "https://bank.example.test/login?fixture=synthetic#marker"
}

### Get own session — 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/session/{{sessionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{browserToken}}

### Export redacted records — 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/threat/logs/export
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
